      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermal exposure can promote the formation or evolution of local chemical ordering in high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12806431::chunk::004::conclusion::d17597a177"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid quenching from the high-temperature BCC state minimizes diffusion and local chemical ordering in Cr39Co18Fe18Ni18Al7.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Holding Cr39Co18Fe18Ni18Al7 at 600–700°C long enough will allow local chemical ordering to develop.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12806431::chunk::004::conclusion::d17597a177",
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The phase evolution is driven by LCO clusters arising from an interplay between magnetic interactions and sluggish atomic diffusion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12806431::chunk::004::conclusion::d17597a177",
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high Cr content accentuates magnetic interactions relevant to phase evolution.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "LCO clusters destabilize the metastable high-temperature BCC state during cooling.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "LCO clusters act as precursors and nucleation sites for secondary ordered phases.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The secondary ordered phase may be B2-like or another ordered derivative.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Local ordered regions lower the free energy relative to the homogeneous BCC state.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The local free-energy reduction caused by ordering leads to nucleation and growth of a secondary phase.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower annealing temperatures can favor decomposition into ordered B2 and disordered BCC phases in a related Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid quenching preserves the high-temperature BCC phase in Cr39Co18Fe18Ni18Al7.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Intermediate-temperature holds will produce detectable LCO and secondary ordered phases absent from rapidly quenched samples.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12806431::chunk::004::conclusion::d17597a177",
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The thermally induced structural changes may be accompanied by changes in magnetic properties.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
